      content:
          '- **Injury Mechanism**: Fall down 4 stairs at home. Struck chin on railing, causing forceful cervical hyperextension. No loss of consciousness. Immediate bilateral hand and arm weakness with preserved ability to walk.\n- **Imaging**: MRI C-spine: severe degenerative stenosis at C4-5 (AP canal diameter 7 mm), disc osteophyte complex, ligamentum flavum hypertrophy. T2 hyperintense signal within the central cord at C4-5 level (no hemorrhage on gradient echo — pure edema pattern, favorable prognostic sign). CT: no fracture.\n- **Hospital Course**: Managed conservatively per neurosurgery — rigid cervical collar x 6 weeks. No surgical decompression recommended at this time (debatable — will discuss). Neurological exam has been slowly improving since admission.\n- **Current Functional Status**: Ambulatory with rolling walker on level surfaces. Requires supervision on stairs. Bilateral hand weakness severely limits ADLs — cannot button clothes, manipulate zippers, hold utensils, write, or open containers. Can feed himself with built-up utensil handles. Bladder: mild urgency and frequency, no retention (post-void residual 60 mL). Bowel: continent, mild constipation.\n- **Pain**: Neck pain 4/10 (muscular). Bilateral burning dysesthesia in hands 5/10 — worse at night.\n- **PMH**: Cervical spondylosis (known for years — never symptomatic until now), hypertension, type 2 diabetes (A1c 7.8%), benign prostatic hyperplasia, mild osteoarthritis bilateral knees.\n- **Wife\'s Condition**: Stage IV breast cancer with bone metastases (spine, pelvis, ribs). Currently receiving palliative chemotherapy (capecitabine). Requires assistance with medication management, meal preparation, transportation to oncology appointments, and emotional support. Previously, the patient performed all these tasks.\n- **Social**: Retired auto mechanic, age 62. Married 35 years. One adult son lives 3 hours away. Medicare insurance. Modest fixed income (Social Security). Single-story home with 4 exterior steps (where the fall occurred).\n- **Medications**: Lisinopril 10 mg daily, metformin 500 mg BID, tamsulosin 0.4 mg QHS, gabapentin 300 mg TID (started for hand dysesthesia), acetaminophen 1000 mg Q8H PRN.',
